	<h1>Irene Iodice</h1>


	<img src="{{ base }}/images/bio.jpeg" align="left"  width="33%" height="36%" style="margin: 0px 30px 10px 0px;"/> <p>
    I am an Assistant Professor of Economics at
    <strong>City St George's, University of London</strong>
    and a CESifo Research Network Affiliate.
    My research lies at the intersection of
    <strong>international trade and industrial organisation</strong>,
    with a focus on how trade policy, regulations, and technical standards
    shape firms' sourcing decisions, production networks, and responses to globalisation.
    </p>

  <div style="clear:both; margin-top:0.75rem;"></div>	
 
  <p style="text-align:left;">
    My current research asks how rules of origin and technical standards
    reshape global sourcing networks, and when coordination across countries
    delivers gains that unilateral policy cannot.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:1.4rem; text-align:left;">
    You can contact me at
    <a href="mailto:irene.iodice@city.ac.uk">irene.iodice@city.ac.uk</a>.
</p>
	
